      "say": "On Azure Kubernetes Service, in the client's own Azure subscription, in one region near the plants. It's entirely private: engineers reach it over the company network with their Azure AD login, and there's no public endpoint. The cluster has four node pools: a system pool, an apps pool for the FastAPI API, reranker and NGINX ingress, a larger ingestion pool for the Celery parsing and OCR workers that scales down when the queue empties, and an Elasticsearch pool for the three data nodes on premium SSDs. Everything around it goes through private endpoints: Azure OpenAI, the container registry, Key Vault, blob storage for the PDFs, and managed Redis and PostgreSQL, so plant data never leaves the private network. We run dev, staging and production. We chose AKS because we self-host Elasticsearch and the reranker and the platform team already ran it. The honest gap is a single region, which the business accepted for an internal tool.",
      "numbers": "One region; 4 node pools; 3 Elasticsearch data nodes on premium SSD; 3 to 10 API pods; 3 environments (dev, staging, production).",
