      "say": "The architecture has two halves. Ingestion runs in the background: a Celery job parses each PDF, chunks it along its headings, embeds the chunks and writes them into Elasticsearch with metadata. At question time, a LangGraph flow rewrites follow-ups, runs hybrid search filtered by the user's permissions, reranks thirty candidates to five, grades whether they answer the question, and then generates a cited answer, all served by FastAPI on AKS. I chose the models by testing on our 300-question golden set. GPT-4o writes answers because it followed the answer-only-from-sources rule best. GPT-4o-mini does rewriting and grading, where speed and cost matter more than depth. text-embedding-3-small scored within a point of BGE-large, and only about two points behind OpenAI's large model at half its storage. bge-reranker-base was chosen because the larger one gained a point for double the latency. And everything runs on Azure over a private endpoint, which is also why the reranker is self-hosted.",
